        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"stendhal-le-rouge-et-le-noir-c1a7b480d862dce2\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.97,\"analysis\":\"The marquis directly avows that he loves or is fond of Abbé Pirard, extending his preceding statement of esteem. The wording presents an attitude as true; it does not itself undertake a relational commitment, and there is no evidence that it is a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"French « aimer » here may denote strong personal liking or regard rather than romantic love, and the avowal may also serve to ingratiate the marquis with Pirard before the employment offer. Those qualifications do not alter its dominant truth-conditional force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"The Marquis de La Mole directly says « je vous aime » to Abbé Pirard during their first meeting.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The marquis moves from « Je vous estime » to the stronger « je vous aime », despite having just met Pirard, after being impressed by his clear and useful legal work. The immediate offer of a highly paid secretaryship gives the avowal a strategic and affiliative setting, but the core words still function as an assertion of personal affection or strong liking. The proposed employment terms and promise to preserve Pirard's parish are separate practical assurances rather than commitment force inherent in « je vous aime ».\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"« Je vous estime, et j'oserais ajouter, quoique vous voyant pour la première fois, je vous aime. »\",\"supports\":\"The coordination with « Je vous estime » and the concessive acknowledgment that this is their first meeting support an explicit avowal of the marquis's present attitude (high T).\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Immediately afterward the marquis asks, « Voulez-vous être mon secrétaire » and offers a large salary.\",\"supports\":\"The utterance occurs while the marquis is recruiting Pirard and may have an ingratiating or affiliative purpose, but that contextual purpose does not itself give the love clause undertaking force.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Pirard's concise written work has just clarified the marquis's legal affairs, after the marquis explains his difficulty finding competent, serious assistance.\",\"supports\":\"The marquis's newly formed admiration has a concrete basis and makes « je vous aime » intelligible as strong approval or fondness rather than romantic love.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The utterance is introduced with the deliberative hedge « j'oserais ajouter » rather than as an involuntary blurting or reflex.\",\"supports\":\"This supports a considered avowal and provides no positive evidence for expressive/reflexive force (E=0).\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is located in Chapter XXX of Stendhal's Le Rouge et le Noir and is tagged as an affirmative present-tense explicit love expression.\",\"supports\":\"Confirms the identified occurrence and its grammatical presentation as a current affirmative attitude.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. The recruitment strategy, social register, and non-romantic sense of « aimer » are contextual qualifications rather than missing dimensions of core force.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
